---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/common/PageHead.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy and enquiries">
  <article class="max-w-content mx-auto px-4 py-12 prose">
    <PageHead title="Privacy and enquiries" lede="What Buyersite saves when you read or send a sourcing brief." />
    <h2 class="mt-8">Your enquiry</h2>
    <p>When you send an enquiry, Buyersite saves your email address, optional name and company, product requirements, the selected article and its source references, your selected questions, and any permitted landing-page and campaign labels. The site owner uses this record to review and respond to your sourcing request. Submitting does not send a message to a supplier, place an order or confirm a quotation.</p>
    <h2 class="mt-8">Reading statistics</h2>
    <p>We count page views and actions such as opening an article, searching and preparing an enquiry. These are daily totals by page. Our analytics do not store your email, question text, search terms, full referrer, IP address or a visitor identifier. We honour Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control. Short-lived hashed request buckets help limit automated abuse and expire separately.</p>
    <p>Within the current tab, the first page you visit and limited campaign labels can be retained until you submit an enquiry or close the tab. We do not retain this attribution when Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control is enabled. A brief you choose to prepare is also kept in this tab so that its selected article, questions and requirements can move to the enquiry form; contact details and conversation transcripts are not saved in that draft.</p>
    <h2 class="mt-8">Sourcing assistant</h2>
    <p>The source notebook searches published facts and returns their original references. If a conversational sourcing service is available, the question you choose to send and its selected article context are passed to that service. Preparing a brief does not submit it: the enquiry form lets you review the details and consent before sending. Commercial terms must be confirmed directly with the supplier.</p>
    <h2 class="mt-8">Access and corrections</h2>
    <p>Enquiries are visible to the site owner and authorized operators. You can request access, correction or deletion by sending an enquiry marked “Privacy request”, using the email address on your original record. Theme preferences may be stored in your browser. Enquiry receipts stay in the current browser tab to prevent duplicate submissions.</p>
    <p class="mt-8"><a href="/enquiry">Contact the Buyersite editorial desk</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
